{"Negative cursor offsets in the optimized pagination path are used directly in queryset slicing, allowing request-controlled cursors to return records outside the intended pagination window": 0.9629297852516174, "Optimized pagination is enabled by a user-controlled flag (optimized_pagination=true query parameter), allowing clients to opt into a different pagination code path by toggling a GET parameter": 0.8255600333213806, "A crafted audit-log request with optimized_pagination=true and a negative/forged cursor can force the endpoint into negative-offset logic instead of the established DateTimePaginator path": 0.961665153503418, "Inconsistent authorization/pagination behavior on the audit-log endpoint can cause record duplication or skipping across pages": 0.795395016670227, "Possible exposure of audit-log entries outside the intended page window due to the pagination bypass": 0.8902637362480164}